<title>UK: INCO optimistic over Sudbury labour talks.</title>
<headline>INCO optimistic over Sudbury labour talks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian metal producer Inco Ltd is optimistic that labour talks at its Sudbury Ontario operations will be settled amicably, company President Scott M. Hand.</p>
<p>&quot;We are in discussions right now, and we are hopeful that we will resolve it without any labour stoppage,&quot; Hand said in an interview.</p>
<p>Sudbury is Inco's largest division and produces 230 million lbs of nickel each year. The current contract ends on May 31.</p>
<p>&quot;We and the union have exchanged positions, we have had a lot of lengthy discussions, but as of this moment the real tough bargaining starts about mid-May,&quot; Hand said.</p>
<p>--Martin Hayes, London Newsroom 44 171 542 8080</p>
</text>
